              "text": "Several boutique law firms in Brisbane’s Southside (specifically in **Mount Gravatt, Upper Mount Gravatt, and Sunnybank**) cater to Family Law and Wills & Estates with transparent fee structures. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Life Law Solutions (Mount Gravatt East)\n* **Location:** 22 Carrara Street, Mount Gravatt East (servicing Upper Mt Gravatt and surrounding Southside suburbs).\n* **Practice Areas:** Family Law, Divorce & Property Settlement, Wills & Estate Planning, Estate Administration.\n* **Pricing & Fee Options:**\n  * **Free Initial Assessment:** Offers a complimentary **15-minute phone assessment** for Wills & Estate Planning and Deceased Estate Administration.\n  * **Fixed-Fee Wills:** Provides scoped fixed-fee packages for standard wills, Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOA), and estate bundles.\n  * **Deferred Fees:** Partnered with **JustFund** (a specialized Australian family law finance provider). This enables eligible family law clients to access a credit line covering legal costs with **no repayments until final property settlement**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Ian W. Bartels & Associates (Mount Gravatt)\n* **Location:** Logan Road, Upper Mount Gravatt / Mount Gravatt.\n* **Practice Areas:** Family Law, Matrimonial Property Disputes, Wills & Estates.\n* **Pricing & Fee Options:**\n  * **Fixed-Fee Wills:** Features a streamlined **\"one-visit economical Will service\"** with upfront fixed fees for standard wills and Powers of Attorney.\n  * **Cost-Conscious Family Law:** Operates as a local boutique practice offering direct solicitor handling to keep overheads low compared to CBD firms.\n\n---\n\n### 3. KLS Legal (Sunnybank)\n* **Location:** Shop 16B, Sunny Park Shopping Centre, 342 McCullough Street, Sunnybank.\n* **Practice Areas:** Family Law (separation, divorce, financial agreements, parenting), Compensation, General Litigation.\n* **Pricing & Fee Options:**\n  * **Free Consultation:** Actively advertises **free initial consultations** for new matters to assess case viability and options.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Denovo Lawyers (Sunnybank Hills / Servicing Mt Gravatt)\n* **Location:** Sunnybank Hills (regularly serving both Sunnybank and Mt Gravatt clients).\n* **Practice Areas:** Family Law, Wills & Estates, Property/Conveyancing, Business Law.\n* **Pricing & Fee Options:**\n  * **Fixed-Fee Estate Planning:** Offers transparent, fixed pricing for standard wills, Powers of Attorney, and basic probate matters to avoid open-ended hourly billing.\n  * **Alternative Pricing:** Transparent quotes provided at intake for family law negotiations and consent orders.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Times Lawyers (Sunnybank)\n* **Location:** Level 1, Times Square (250 McCullough St) and Sunnybank Square (309 Mains Rd), Sunnybank.\n* **Practice Areas:** Family Law, Wills & Estates, Conveyancing (multilingual team: English, Mandarin, Cantonese).\n* **Pricing & Fee Options:**\n  * **Transparent Consultation / Quoting:** Offers clear fixed-rate initial consultations and stage-by-stage quoted costs for wills and simple family law documentation rather than unpredictable time-billing.\n\n---\n\n### 6. VM Family Law (Servicing Mount Gravatt / Brisbane South)\n* **Location:** Dedicated family law firm with southside coverage (including Mount Gravatt consultations).\n* **Practice Areas:** Family Law, Separation, Domestic Violence, Property Settlements.\n* **Pricing & Fee Options:**\n  * **Deferred Fee Option:** Officially partnered with **JustFund**, allowing approved property-settlement clients to defer 100% of their legal fees until their property or asset pool is finalized and paid out.\n  * **Fixed-Fee Scoping:** Offers fixed pricing for defined steps like Consent Orders and Financial Agreements.\n\n---\n\n### How \"Deferred Fees\" Work in Queensland Family Law & Estates\n* **Family Law:** Under Queensland professional conduct rules and the *Family Law Act*, solicitors are strictly prohibited from taking a percentage cut of your property settlement (contingency fees). Instead, firms provide deferred access by partnering with legal finance providers (e.g., **JustFund**) or by entering into a formal agreement allowing legal fees to be deducted from the property settlement trust account upon sale/transfer of assets.\n* **Wills & Estates:** For deceased estate administration or probate, most boutique firms will agree to defer professional fees so that they are **paid directly out of estate funds** once the assets are liquidated or the grant of probate is issued.",
